{"term":"epidemic","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:733e6dd5830dc71f61","definition":"A widespread disease that affects many humans in a population.","example":"At that time, the city [Christiania, now Oslo] was in the grip of a cholera epidemic, and victims were dying at the rate of 60 a day. Bradshaw contracted the disease, and died on September 6 [1853].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1947938ec482b2163b","definition":"An occurrence of a disease or disorder in a human population at a frequency higher than that expected in a given time period; an episode of outbreak and subsequent high prevalence.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dad508852918539cb3","definition":"A heightened occurrence of anything harmful.","example":"Even before the pandemic, the United States surgeon general, Vivek Murthy, said the country was experiencing an “epidemic of loneliness,” driven by the accelerated pace of life and the spread of technology into all of our social interactions.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, colloquial","register":"broadly, colloquial","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d86b543a9bad55f06d","definition":"The spreading of an idea or belief amongst a population.","example":"Lord Avonleigh was at once liberated from his imprisonment, well prepared to be considered, and to consider himself, a martyr to the cause of loyalty; and as the services of the rich nobleman,...his claims to notice and favour were most graciously acknowledged. Accordingly, he returned to his seat in a little fever of royal devotedness—it was the fashionable epidemic; and who coming from Whitehall could be without it?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5d4ca5951b085c5b8c","definition":"Of, related to, or being an epidemic: a widespread outbreak of disease in humans.","example":"The tetany that was epidemic among slaved children was actually the result of severe calcium, magnesium, and vitamin D deficiency caused by chronic malnutrition.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic","ecoepidemic","endemoepidemic","epidemically","epidemicity","nonepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6abb623b2253fc3388","definition":"Like an epidemic: widespread in a bad way.","example":"Epidemic hysteria occurred upon the incumbent’s reelection.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["common","ubiquitous","common","disseminated","far-flung","extensive","pervasive","predominant","prevailing","prevalent","regnant","rife","spread out","systemic","ubiquitous","universal","widespread"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic","postepidemic","pre-epidemic","preepidemic","pseudoepidemic","subepidemic","syndemic","virgin soil epidemic","hyperepidemic","ecoepidemic","endemoepidemic","epidemically","epidemicity","nonepidemic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˌɛpɪˈdɛmɪk/"},"wordFamily":["antiepidemic","epicurve","epidemic curve","epidemiclike","iatroepidemic","infodemic","interepidemic","microepidemic","midepidemic","panepidemic","post-epidemic